  "authoringNote": "C01 adds six calendar months to the encounter date: 2026-03-15 plus six months is 2026-09-15 (day 15 exists, no clamping), and the upper bound is inclusive, so the final order dated 2026-09-15 is within the interval. It follows the encounter and both state SYN-PRAC-0001, so R04 passes with six citations. This is 184 elapsed days, so a fixed 183-day duration would wrongly reject it; calendar-month arithmetic is required. The receipt (2026-09-16T17:00:00Z) is after the order date span 2026-09-14T10:00Z to 2026-09-16T12:00Z (C06), so R05 passes. R01, R02, R03, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. No condition holds outside R06 and R10, every parent set is empty and the state is ready_for_review; human acceptance remains a separate action.",
